# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
#
# Terminal preset rule. systemd's built-in fallback policy for a unit that
# matches no rule is "enable", so without this every package pulled in by
# Packages= -- directly or as a dependency -- would be started at boot inside
# the CVM, with no diff to 80-dstack.preset and nothing for a reviewer to see.
#
# This inverts that to opt-in, matching the Yocto backend, where a service is
# only started if a recipe sets SYSTEMD_SERVICE/SYSTEMD_AUTO_ENABLE. Anything
# that must run in the guest belongs in 80-dstack.preset, which is ordered
# before this file and therefore wins.
disable *
